# Content and copy

Full guidance in `docs/spec/04-content-and-bilingual.md`.

## Voice: assessor-plain

Write the way a good service assessor writes a report. Specific, unhurried, no persuasion.

Banned in product UI: just, simply, easily, seamlessly, powerful, robust, leverage, unlock,
supercharge, effortlessly. Landing-page voice must not appear past sign-in.

No congratulation. An index of 82 is a fact, not an achievement.

## Microcopy

- A button states what happens; the toast echoes the same verb.
- Destructive actions name the object and the consequence.
- Errors identify the field and the fix, and do not apologise.
- Empty states are an invitation plus why it matters, with one action.
- No decimals on the index or on percentages. Dates as `30 Jul 2026`.

## Bilingual

- Prefer `next-intl` / existing i18n messages for UI strings.
- ICU-style messages with named arguments; never concatenate for plurals.
- Machine-translated Welsh must not reach an export.
- User content (rationales, evidence titles) is stored as authored and never machine-translated.

